<title>SWEDEN: POLL-Atlas Copco H1 profit seen flat.</title>
<headline>POLL-Atlas Copco H1 profit seen flat.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish industrial engineer Atlas Copco  was expected to post a profit after financial items of 1.55 billion  crowns for the first half of 1997, unchanged from a year ago, a Reuters  poll of 10 analysts found on Friday.</p>
<p>Forecasts varied between 1.38-1.60 billion crowns.</p>
<p>For the full year analysts estimated the company would post a profit  after financial items of 3.21 billion crowns.</p>
<p>Analysts interviewed for the poll were from Aros, CI Nordic Securities,  Den Danske Bank, Den Norske Bank, Fischer Partners, James Capel, Lehman  Brothers, Matteus, Paribas, Penser, Swedbank, and Ohman.</p>
<p>Atlas Copco will release its half year results on August 6. PROFIT  AFTER FIN ITEMS (Mln SKR)</p>
<p>		     AVG	   RANGE	    NO OF ANALYSTS</p>
<p> H1 1997	  1,552	1,383-1,600		10</p>
<p> Full yr '97    3,206	2,898-3,455		12</p>
<p> Full yr '98    3,629	3,286-3,850		12</p>
<p>EARNINGS PER SHARE (SKR)</p>
<p>		    AVG	   RANGE	     NO OF ANALYSTS</p>
<p> Full yr '97   11.00	 10.00-12.00		11</p>
<p> Full yr '98   12.50	 11.40-13.50		11</p>
